Round 135 is complete and live — stamp 1787600699 confirmed at 13:26:50. (The two "failed" task notices are just my own stuck waiter loops being killed — they had hit the documented self-matching-pgrep trap; nothing of the round failed.)

**What this round did.** The queue head from r134: the two remaining single-owner boxy classes in `buildGalleyWorks` — the galleass's gun deck (31 plain boxes) and the war galley's arrumbada (4). Reading the code found more than boxiness: the gun deck was a slab floating between two clamps with **no athwartships beams at all**, and the arrumbada's platform posts were gated on `S.gunDeck`, a field no arrumbada hull carries — dead code since the branch was written, so the galley's bow platform stood on nothing forward of the apostis.

**The rebuild continues r134's carried-structure law one storey up.** Tapered stanchions stand on the apostis rails, clamps ride on their heads, deck beams span clamp to clamp at every stanchion, and the planking lies on the beams — drawn by a new shared `deckGeo` helper whose section carries a V-seam at every plank edge, so seams are geometry with real edges (the snapBand law), with pitch in metres because a deck plank is a real-world width. The screen and breastwork became planking under eased caps at their exact old top lines; the arrumbada got its three beams and its posts.

