Round 167 is complete and live. The summary:

**The queue head — r163's fleet-wide no-rake tier sampling residual — opened and closed, measured before anything was edited.** `linerHouse half()` sampled the shell at u as if x were (u−0.5)·lwl, so inside the rake spans every wall was sized off a station up to a rake's length away; r163 had fixed it only for Queen Mary 2's over-counter record. A new instrument (`build/staging/r167/measure-norake.py`, 241 stations per tier) measured the bias per ship first: nil where the house sits inboard of the rake spans (azzam and steamer, 0.000), sub-metre where a tier edge enters one — titanic +0.054 m at her aft corner, great-eastern +0.081 m, the warship bow tiers +0.22–0.31 m (consumed only by fittings and boats, since turret and flight-deck hulls draw no house walls), and QM2's 1.67 m being exactly the bias her r163 gate already corrected.

**The change:** `half()` now inverts the true deck-edge x by bisection on every hull — the ship gate is deleted, one sampling for the fleet. The instrument re-run confirmed the applied deltas equal the predicted bias to the millimetre, and QM2, azzam, and steamer moved +0.000.

